  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Somalia&apos;s National Security Architecture (SSNSA 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the foundations of SSNSA 2, Integrated Security Fund (ISF) through SSNSA 3 continues to support Somali security sector reform through technical advisory services to the FGS security ministries and selected Federal Member States (FMS) administrations. It also introduces African Union Support and Stabilisation Mission in Somalia (AUSSOM) ? transition advisers, funded via a Technical Assistance Facility (TAF), to deliver short-term, targeted support aligned with SSNSA 3 objectives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Security Sector Coherence: Align FGS and FMS security strategies with Presidential objectives and SSDP goals to ensure coordinated, integrated security frameworks and proactive alignment with priority initiatives.
Strategic Planning and Leadership Support: Strengthen Somali leadership capacity in implementing long-term security strategies, promote accountability, and foster international engagement aligned with Somali priorities.
UK Influence and Insights: Enhance UK access to Somali decision-makers, ensuring mutual understanding of strategic security planning and strengthening UK policy influence.
Integrated Delivery: Foster collaboration among HMG and non-HMG partners under Somali leadership to improve international security coordination.</narrative>
  </description>
